Compile ricmoo/QRCode as C17, for GCC 15

Applied by scripts/patch_simulator.py after 0002. Task H1 (#72).

run_simulator.py (the simulator library's build script): QRCode's C dialect
  ricmoo/QRCode 0.0.1 is a registry dependency of [env:simulator]
  (platformio.project.ini lib_deps), not part of the simulator library. Its
  src/qrcode.h does `typedef unsigned char bool;` (with `false` and `true`
  constants) when compiled as C. GCC 15 compiles C as C23 by default, where
  bool is a keyword, so qrcode.c fails to compile ("'bool' cannot be defined
  via 'typedef'") on Ubuntu 26.04 / GitHub's ubuntu-latest. GCC 13 (Ubuntu
  24.04) defaults to gnu17 and is unaffected, as is the device toolchain.
  qrcode.h itself cannot be patched by this mechanism: patch_simulator.py
  only patches the simulator's own git checkout, pinned by commit, while
  QRCode is an unpacked registry archive. The simulator's build script
  already adjusts other libraries' builders (the GfxRenderer screen text
  hook), so the fix goes there: QRCode's builder alone gets -std=gnu17 in
  its CFLAGS. Our own files and every other library keep the compiler's
  default dialect. Libraries in libdeps are created in sorted name order,
  so "QRCode" exists when the "simulator" library's script runs; if it is
  not found the script says so and the build goes on unchanged.

diff --git a/run_simulator.py b/run_simulator.py
index 3e23c3a..1633187 100644
--- a/run_simulator.py
+++ b/run_simulator.py
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@ Handles two things automatically when this lib is included as a lib_dep:
    drawText() reports its strings to the simulator (CROSSPOINT_SIM_SCREEN_TEXT).
    The firmware checkout is not modified.
 
+5. Compiles the QRCode library's C files as C17 (-std=gnu17). Its qrcode.h
+   typedefs bool, which C23 (the default C dialect of GCC 15) rejects.
+
 This file can be loaded more than once in the same PlatformIO process:
 - once from this library's `library.json` build hook
 - again indirectly when a consuming firmware repo adds the separate
@@ -108,6 +111,24 @@ def _add_screen_text_hook():
 _add_screen_text_hook()
 
 
+# --- C dialect of ricmoo/QRCode ---
+
+def _qrcode_c17():
+    from SCons.Script import DefaultEnvironment
+
+    # QRCode's qrcode.h has `typedef unsigned char bool;` for C, an error in C23,
+    # which GCC 15 uses by default. Compile that library alone as C17. Libraries
+    # in libdeps are created in name order, so QRCode's builder exists here.
+    for lb in DefaultEnvironment().get("__PIO_LIB_BUILDERS", None) or []:
+        if os.path.basename(lb.path) == "QRCode":
+            lb.env.AppendUnique(CFLAGS=["-std=gnu17"])
+            return
+    print("Simulator: QRCode library not found; its C dialect is not set")
+
+
+_qrcode_c17()
+
+
 # --- run_simulator custom target ---
 
